    "title": "This Robot Walked Off Its Own Assembly Line 🤖 #shorts",
    "description": "No one carried it. No remote control. 🤖\n\nOn September 8 in Guangzhou, XPeng's IRON humanoid robot walked off its own production line by itself. More than 80% of the line's core assembly is automated, and XPeng is targeting mass production by the end of 2026. Its walk is so human that at its launch people accused XPeng of hiding a person inside, so the company cut its leg open on stage to show the motors and metal underneath.\n\nWould you let one walk around your house? 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
